  "usage_note": "In the first sense **exercise** is uncountable: *get more exercise*, *a lot of exercise*. Use the countable form only for particular movements (*leg exercises*) or tasks (*a grammar exercise*). The usual verb is **get**; British English also says *do some exercise* and *take exercise*. You do not **make** exercise.",
  "learner_errors": [
    {
      "incorrect": "I need to do more exercises.",
      "correct": "I need to get more exercise.",
      "note": "For physical activity in general, **exercise** is uncountable."
    },
    {
      "incorrect": "I make exercise every day.",
      "correct": "I exercise every day.",
      "note": "Use the verb **exercise**, or **get exercise**; not **make exercise**."
    }
  ],
